1. PAPUA NEW GUINEA OVERVIEW
Papua New Guinea’s population has passed the 10 million mark. The 2024 National Population
Census counted 10,185,363 people in PNG on Census night.
This represents an increase of 40% (2,910,039 people) in PNG’s population count since 2011
(7 ,275,324)
The average annual growth rate over the past 13 years, since the 2011 Census, was 2.6%.
Annual growth rate since the 2011 Census is higher (3.1%) but is likely to be artificially inflated
because of non-demographic factors such as higher undercounting in 2000 and improvements to
the 2011 and 2024 Census coverage methods.
More males than females were counted in PNG on Census night (52.4% and 47 .6% of the total
population, respectively). This represents approximately 110 males to every 100 females.
The average number of people per household was 5 for PNG.
Since the first official census in 1980, five years after independence, there have been an additional
7 .2 million people added from 3.0 million in the last 44 years
